{"id":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter","module":"concurrent.interpreters","qualname":"Interpreter","name":"Interpreter","kind":"class","parent":null,"signatures":["Interpreter(id)"],"doc":"A single Python interpreter.\n\nAttributes:\n\n\"id\" - the unique process-global ID number for the interpreter\n\"whence\" - indicates where the interpreter was created\n\nIf the interpreter wasn't created by this module\nthen any method that modifies the interpreter will fail,\ni.e. .close(), .prepare_main(), .exec(), and .call()","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/concurrent.interpreters.html#concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["not WASI"],"source":{"path":"Lib/concurrent/interpreters/__init__.py","line":96},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter.call","module":"concurrent.interpreters","qualname":"Interpreter.call","name":"call","kind":"method","parent":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter","signatures":["Interpreter.call(callable, /, *args, **kwargs)"],"doc":"Call the object in the interpreter with given args/kwargs.\n\nNearly all callables, args, kwargs, and return values are\nsupported.  All \"shareable\" objects are supported, as are\n\"stateless\" functions (meaning non-closures that do not use\nany globals).  This method will fall back to pickle.\n\nIf the callable raises an exception then the error display\n(including full traceback) is sent back between the interpreters\nand an ExecutionFailed exception is raised, much like what\nhappens with Interpreter.exec().","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/concurrent.interpreters.html#concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter.call","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["not WASI"],"source":{"path":"Lib/concurrent/interpreters/__init__.py","line":231},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter.call_in_thread","module":"concurrent.interpreters","qualname":"Interpreter.call_in_thread","name":"call_in_thread","kind":"method","parent":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter","signatures":["Interpreter.call_in_thread(callable, /, *args, **kwargs)"],"doc":"Return a new thread that calls the object in the interpreter.\n\nThe return value and any raised exception are discarded.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/concurrent.interpreters.html#concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter.call_in_thread","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["not WASI"],"source":{"path":"Lib/concurrent/interpreters/__init__.py","line":246},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter.close","module":"concurrent.interpreters","qualname":"Interpreter.close","name":"close","kind":"method","parent":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter","signatures":["Interpreter.close()"],"doc":"Finalize and destroy the interpreter.\n\nAttempting to destroy the current interpreter results\nin an InterpreterError.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/concurrent.interpreters.html#concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter.close","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["not WASI"],"source":{"path":"Lib/concurrent/interpreters/__init__.py","line":187},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
{"id":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter.exec","module":"concurrent.interpreters","qualname":"Interpreter.exec","name":"exec","kind":"method","parent":"concurrent.interpreters/Interpreter","signatures":["Interpreter.exec(code, /)"],"doc":"Run the given source code in the interpreter.\n\nThis is essentially the same as calling the builtin \"exec\"\nwith this interpreter, using the __dict__ of its __main__\nmodule as both globals and locals.\n\nThere is no return value.\n\nIf the code raises an unhandled exception then an ExecutionFailed\nexception is raised, which summarizes the unhandled exception.\nThe actual exception is discarded because objects cannot be\nshared between interpreters.\n\nThis blocks the current Python thread until done.  During\nthat time, the previous interpreter is allowed to run\nin other threads.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/concurrent.interpreters.html#concurrent.interpreters.Interpreter.exec","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["not WASI"],"source":{"path":"Lib/concurrent/interpreters/__init__.py","line":203},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
